{
  "dom_id": "step-q332627",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613?$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =9[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1(10)+1(8) \\\\ 1(10)+1(8)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
